  "title": "Horizontal AI applications market map (ICP, wedge, pricing, density)",
  "content": "## Objective\nCreate a structured market map of the **Horizontal Application layer** (cross-industry AI copilots/apps) across: **general copilots, coding, customer support, sales/marketing, knowledge work, design/content, meetings, search**. For each major product (or product cluster), capture: **ICP**, **workflow wedge**, **pricing model**, and **competitive density signals**.\n\n## Output format (what we will produce)\n- A single consolidated **markdown table** (or set of tables by segment) with columns:\n  - Segment\n  - Company / Product\n  - ICP (role, company size, industry tilt)\n  - Workflow wedge (entry point + integrations + “why now”)\n  - Pricing model (seat-based, usage-based, bundles, add-ons; list price if available)\n  - Competitive density signals (see rubric below)\n  - Notes / sources\n\n## Competitive density rubric (signals to collect)\n- **# of credible direct competitors** (≥5 = high)\n- **Incumbent bundling pressure** (Microsoft/Google/Salesforce/Adobe/etc.)\n- **Switching costs / data gravity** (high if deeply embedded into existing systems)\n- **Distribution advantage** (pre-install, marketplace, default-in-suite)\n- **Model commoditization risk** (features easily replicated vs proprietary workflows/data)\n\n## Approach\n1) Define a consistent schema + density rubric (to reduce ambiguity).\n2) Parallelize segment research via sub-agents (each returns a filled segment table with citations).\n3) Synthesize into one coherent horizontal-layer map with cross-segment comparisons and density takeaways.",
